\subtree{
  \title{Decision}
  \p{Model structures are theorems, never definitions. The \strong{named mountain} is \code{HasColimits Kan} (and limits): an interface one-liner whose proof is the Segal-category analogue of HTT 4.2.4.1 — homotopy colimits of Kan complexes (Bousfield–Kan / Hirschhorn) are colimits in the Segal category \code{Kan} in the sense of → \ref{dec-up-0004}, established through the identification of derived mapping spaces. The Segal-native route is Simpson's \em{Homotopy Theory of Higher Categories} (limits and colimits in \code{nCAT} with discrete object sets). Everything downstream depends on it: cocompleteness of \code{PSh(C)}, coends, composites of profunctors (→ \ref{dec-ft-0002}), Kan extensions along Yoneda, the Kleisli VDC∞s and composition products of → \ref{dec-sp-0009}. It is scheduled by name in → \ref{rm-0000}. Other milestones, in the order they unblock things: Kan–Quillen (from the inventory if present); Reedy/Bergner for Segal categories (needed for \ref{at-kr-0011} and rectification); Segal categories ≃ complete Segal spaces (Bergner) as \ref{at-sp-0005}; complete Segal spaces ≃ quasi-categories (Joyal–Tierney) and Cisinski's \code{S} — optional, opens Kerodon/HTT as a source; dendroidal Segal spaces ≃ Lurie's ∞-operads (Heuts–Hinich–Moerdijk) — optional; style B ≃ style A for VDC∞ (\ref{at-rt-0009}) — optional.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Status}
